configurations, and prompt templates are detailed in Appendix A . 5 Experimental Setup 5.1 Models We report four model variants from this work: the unmodified Qwen3-4B base , SFT checkpoint, and two RLVR checkpoints RLVR-dense (Eq. 1 dense weights) and RLVR-sparse (sparse weights). For external context we evaluate five open-weights 7B math-specialised models, Abel-7B-002, DeepSeek-Math-7B-RL, Eurus-2-7B-PRIME, MAmmoTH2-7B-Plus and Qwen2.5-Math-7B-Instruct ( Shao et al., 2024 ; Yang et al., 2024 ; Cui et al., 2025 ; Yue et al., 2024 ) , and six frontier commercial APIs from the DeepSeek and Gemini families. Per-model breakdowns of the external comparators are deferred to Appendix G ; in the main paper we summarise them as a best-7B row and a frontier-API range. For the cross-family replication of § 6.6 we repeat the pipeline on Gemma-3-4B. 5.2 Benchmarks Counterexample (in-domain, n=201). Our held-out test split (§ 3.3 ), stratified by domain. The strict scoring criterion is q ¬ = 1 ∧ s hyp = n hyp q_{
